                    <h3>What is a Fixed Deposit?</h3>
                    <p>
                        A Fixed Deposit is a savings option where you deposit a lump sum amount with a bank or financial institution for a selected period. The deposit earns interest according to the applicable rate and terms of the institution.
                    </p>

                    <ul>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>Choose a deposit amount according to your savings plan.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>Select a suitable investment period based on your financial needs.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>Earn interest according to the applicable rate and deposit terms.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>Can be used for planned savings and different financial goals.</span></li>
                    </ul>

                    <p>
                        Fixed Deposits can be considered for goals such as building planned savings, keeping funds for future expenses, creating a financial reserve, or planning for other short-term and long-term requirements.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Before choosing a Fixed Deposit, consider the interest rate, tenure, maturity amount, premature withdrawal conditions, taxation, applicable charges, and other terms offered by the financial institution. Interest rates and conditions may vary depending on the institution and deposit type.
                    </p>
